5. ARCHITECTURE RULES
============================================================

MVVM — non-negotiable:
  - All ViewModels inherit ObservableObject (CommunityToolkit.Mvvm)
  - Properties decorated with [ObservableProperty]
  - Commands decorated with [RelayCommand]
  - Code-behind: ONLY InitializeComponent() allowed
  - Zero business logic in Views or code-behind
  - View <-> ViewModel binding via BindingContext only
  - Services injected via DI, never instantiated with new()

Dependency Injection (register in MauiProgram.cs):
  - Singleton: DatuBaseaZerbitzua, AutorizazioZerbitzua,
               ArgazkiIgotzeZerbitzua, EncryptionZerbitzua
  - Transient: ViewModels
  - Scoped: not used in MAUI

============================================================
6. ROLE-BASED NAVIGATION — SEPARATE TAB SETS
============================================================

Admin and Employee MUST have completely separate Shell tab sets.
Use Shell routing with role-based conditional loading at login.
NEVER show admin tabs to employees or employee tabs to admins.

Admin tab set (Administratzailea):
  Tab 1 — Txartel Guztiak     (all employee tickets to review)
  Tab 2 — Nire Gastuak        (admin's own expenses, auto-approved)
  Tab 3 — Langile Zerrenda    (employee management)
  Tab 4 — Ezarpenak           (settings / logout)

Employee tab set (Langilea):
  Tab 1 — Nire Txartelak      (my submitted tickets + status)
  Tab 2 — Txartel Berria      (submit new expense ticket)
  Tab 3 — Ezarpenak           (settings / logout)

RULE: Admin's own expense tickets are created directly as
TxartelEgoera.Onartua — no approval workflow needed.
RULE: Employees can NEVER access admin routes, even by URL manipulation.

