7. UX AND USABILITY RULES — CRITICAL
============================================================

The app MUST be intuitive and simple for all users.
Assume users are not tech-savvy. Follow these rules:

General UX:
  - Every screen must have a clear single primary action (one main button)
  - Use plain Basque language — no technical jargon in UI text
  - Loading states: always show a spinner or skeleton for async ops
  - Empty states: always show a friendly message (not a blank screen)
    Example: "Oraindik ez duzu txartelik bidali" (No tickets yet)
  - Confirmation dialogs for destructive actions (delete, reject)
  - Success/error feedback after every user action (Toast/Snackbar)
  - Back navigation always available (never trap the user in a screen)

Forms (ticket submission):
  - Validate inline — show error under the field immediately
  - Required fields marked visually (asterisk or color hint)
  - "Gorde" (Save) button disabled until form is valid
  - Auto-fill date with today's date
  - Amount field: numeric keyboard, 2 decimal places, currency symbol

Ticket list (both roles):
  - Status badge prominently visible (color-coded):
      Zain     -> Amber/yellow badge
      Onartua  -> Green badge
      Ukatua   -> Red badge
  - Most recent tickets at the top (sorted by DataOrdua DESC)
  - Pull-to-refresh on all lists
  - Swipe or tap to open ticket detail

Admin review flow:
  - Detail screen shows full ticket info + photo (if any)
  - Onartu (Approve) and Ukatu (Reject) buttons clearly separated
  - Reject MUST show a text input for reason (AdminOharra)
  - After action: return to list and show result Toast

Photo attachment:
  - Optional on ticket form
  - Show thumbnail preview immediately after selection
  - Clear button to remove selected photo
  - If upload fails: inform user, allow retry, do not block form save

